,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}({x}^{3}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot j\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $3{y}^{2}.$" 13194139543374 17592186576411 false] [17592186262698 1074 "If $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{n}$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\nIn our case, we need to find an expression for the flux across only the part ${C}_{2}$ of the closed curve $C.$ Since this side is perpendicular to the $y$-axis and we require an outward-pointing unit normal vector, we must have $\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{j}.$ \n\n![](images/a8/a83c3476bbe2ed2872ed8938dda59c5d0e6d58d05ecaf662748e7a184a4994a4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}({x}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+3{y}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot \\mathbf{j}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}3{y}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $3{y}^{2}.$" 13194139543374 17592186576411 true] [17592186262699 1071 "![](images/4d/4d9663a0a40f3c3860cce0712e9e9aab41d55251ea15fca33ec663515af57d10.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{3}y\\,i-x{y}^{2}\\,j$ and the rectangle $C,$ shown above. If the flux of $F$ across the side ${C}_{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139543374 17592186576411 false] [17592186262699 1071 "![](images/4d/4d9663a0a40f3c3860cce0712e9e9aab41d55251ea15fca33ec663515af57d10.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)={x}^{3}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-x{y}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ an