-\\mathbf{i})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}-{x}^{3}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $-{x}^{3}y.$" 13194139543374 17592186576411 true] [17592186262700 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=15xy\\,i+5{x}^{2}\\,j$ and the circle $C$ given by ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25.$ If the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: The outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C$ is $n=\\frac{x}{5}\\,i+\\frac{y}{5}\\,j.$*" 13194139543374 17592186576411 false] [17592186262700 1071 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=15xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+5{x}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and the circle $C$ given by ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25.$ If the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: The outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C$ is $\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{x}{5}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{y}{5}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$*" 13194139543374 17592186576411 true] [17592186262700 1074 "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\n![](images/d3/d3d68329d81150c4a975bae4963d4e480cefaef0f2a0a29a0648c3793e9fb462.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}(15xy\\,i+5{x}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{x}{5}\\,i+\\frac{y}{5}\\,j)\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}3{x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}4{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $4{x}^{2}y.$" 13194139543374 17592186576411 false] [17592186262700 1074 "If $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\mathbf{F